    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (79.36). **Gunnar Henderson** holds the slate\u2019s top efficiency score, benefitting from a premium matchup against Avila, where a 4.91 xERA and favorable park factors provide a massive +16% boost to his base projection. Simultaneously, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is a must-start, leveraging a dynamic platoon advantage against Sears. While the overall lineup is deep, **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Kyle Tucker** (75.35) also anchor the daily production; **Jackson Merrill** specifically benefits from an elite matchup against a struggling Bieber, while **Kyle Tucker** remains locked in despite a tougher matchup, as his base talent carries the score well above the volatility of the opposing starter.\n\nStrategic lineup construction emphasizes the scarcity of stolen bases, as seen in the selection of **Josh Lowe** (68.22) and **Andy Pages** (72.83). Both players gain incremental value from facing pitchers with slow deliveries, facilitating their paths to stolen bases. **Miguel Vargas** (63.96) remains a strong play in the utility slot; while facing a lefty, his elite xwOBA of 0.402 provides a high floor that outweighs typical platoon concerns. On the periphery, **Dominic Smith** was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine, narrowly missing the cut behind **Drake Baldwin** (59.40); ultimately, the optimizer favored **Drake Baldwin**\u2019s higher efficiency projection despite the depth of the bench pool. \n\nRegarding risks, we are monitoring the situation closely as no major weather delays are currently projected for our primary hitters, though we have taken note of the 36% rain risk impacting **Jorge Polanco**, which further justifies his placement on the bench today. Our focus remains on maximizing plate appearances from high-efficiency performers like **Heliot Ramos**, whose matchup against Gordon, T is enhanced by a wind-out factor (+5%) that should boost his power potential. While we have depth in **Jacob Wilson** and **Nasim Nunez**, their scores did not clear the 50-point threshold required to displace the current starters in today\u2019s specific matchup environment.",
